content.text:
The fault is a network delay on the `search`→`geo` connection, and it reaches users through `search` and `frontend`.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "network_delay",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name AS caller, s.service_name AS callee, count(*) n, approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS client_med_ms, approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS server_med_ms, approx_quantile(c.duration,0.95)/1e6 AS client_p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND c.span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "search's client spans to geo take a median of about 1575 ms while geo's server spans take about 0.14 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name AS caller, s.service_name AS callee, count(*) n, approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS client_med_ms, approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS server_med_ms FROM normal_traces c JOIN normal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='search' AND c.span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Before the incident the same search-to-geo call took about 0.46 ms client-side and 0.13 ms server-side."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='geo' AND attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "geo's own server spans stay fast, with p95 about 0.24 ms during the incident, so the extra time sits between the two services."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name AS caller, c.span_name, s.service_name AS callee, count(*) n, approx_quantile(c.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS client_med_ms, approx_quantile(s.duration,0.5)/1e6 AS server_med_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id = c.trace_id WHERE c.service_name='frontend' AND c.span_name='search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "frontend's client spans to search take about 1597 ms median, matching search's server time, so the delay passes straight through to frontend."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

